=>OWASP Findings — Ahmedabad Co-Working Test Site
================================================

Finding 1: Server header reveals software/version banner
OWASP Category: Security Misconfiguration (A05:2021)
Evidence: burp_history.png (response headers pane, "Server:" line —
          e.g. "SimpleHTTP/0.6 Python/3.x")
Fix: Suppress or genericize the Server header at the web server/reverse
     proxy layer; don't run production traffic through Python's
     built-in dev server, which exposes exact language/version info.

Finding 2: Missing security response headers
OWASP Category: Security Misconfiguration (A05:2021)
Evidence: burp_repeater.png (response headers pane — no
          Content-Security-Policy, X-Content-Type-Options,
          X-Frame-Options, Strict-Transport-Security present)
Fix: Add standard security headers (CSP, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff,
     X-Frame-Options: DENY, HSTS) at the server/framework level.

Finding 3: /staff_only/ path accessible despite robots.txt disallow
OWASP Category: Broken Access Control (A01:2021)
Evidence: burp_repeater.png (GET /staff_only/desk_prices.html -> 200 OK
          with internal pricing content returned)
Fix: robots.txt is not an access control mechanism — it's a crawler
     courtesy convention, publicly readable by anyone. Enforce real
     authentication/authorization (e.g., server-side login check or
     network-level restriction) on /staff_only/, and never rely on
     "hidden by omission" paths for anything sensitive.
